{"name":"Pastry Dough","hex":"#faedd5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pastry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A baked food item  made from flour and fat pastes such as pie crust; also tarts, bear claws, napoleons, puff pastries, etc.","The food group formed by the various kinds of pastries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pastry"},{"term":"dough","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick, malleable substance made by mixing flour with other ingredients such as water, eggs, or butter, that is made into a particular form and then baked.","Money."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make into dough."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dough"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pastry","blocks":[{"text":"Pastry is various unleavened doughs, often enriched with fat or eggs. The dough may be called pastry dough. Common pastry dishes include börek, pies, tarts, and turnovers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Making_puff_pastry_%28butter_and_Water_dough_%29_5.jpg/330px-Making_puff_pastry_%28butter_and_Water_dough_%29_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastry","wikidata":"Q477248"},{"title":"Dough","blocks":[{"text":"Dough is a malleable, sometimes elastic paste most commonly made from flour or meal. Dough is typically made by mixing flour with a small amount of water or other liquid, and sometimes includes yeast, other leavening agents, or ingredients such as fats or flavourings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Dough.jpg/330px-Dough.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dough","wikidata":"Q178024"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Antique_1920s_Pittsburgh_Noodle_Machine_company_Pasta_Maker1.jpg/500px-Antique_1920s_Pittsburgh_Noodle_Machine_